Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:29:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/26] [Diffusion] Causal DMD stage: DiT-config local window
 and request-scoped cache geometry

* local_attn_size is read from the DiT config. e00930c read
  self.transformer.model.local_attn_size; the causal DiTs have no .model, so it
  always fell back to -1 (the buffer was sized by sliding_window_num_frames
  even for a configured local window). An explicit realtime KV-buffer override
  (realtime_causal_kv_cache_num_frames) still wins. No shipped model changes
  size: LongLive 2.0 has local_attn_size == sliding_window_num_frames == 32,
  Wan/LingBot have -1.
* Stage caches are reused across requests only when the request's geometry
  matches (layers, global sink, sink tokens, buffer tokens at the request's
  tokens per frame); the stock forward now uses _cache_needs_reinit_for_batch
  like LongLive 2.0 instead of reusing the first request's caches whatever the
  resolution. Same-geometry requests are reset exactly as before.
* _causal_kv_cache_size_for_batch(batch) is the per-request sizing hook
  (request-sized full-history caches for the CausVid/RAVEN profiles); it only
  adds kv_cache_size to the init kwargs when it differs from the stage default.

Tests: config window, realtime override precedence, reinit on resolution/sink/
layer changes, request-sized override.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
